WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:06.100
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.930
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:16.010
Verse 12

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:16.010
So the flower
 petals are 
scattered like
 the snow by
 the passing
 storm

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:19.920
<i>The Master and Queen challenger playoffs</i>

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.220
<i>are a best-of-three, where whoever
takes two matches is declared the winner.</i>

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.980
<i>The Queen playoff will be between 
Inokuma-san and Megumu-chan.</i>

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.170
<i>Two people I played recently
will be going at it in the playoff.</i>

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.110
<b>Stomach hurts 
out of regret</b>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.110
<b>Ugh</b>

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:38.500
<i>And the Master playoff...</i>

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:49.000
<i>So much fidgeting...
He's not used to the kimono.</i>

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.340
<i>But the kimono certainly looks right at home.</i>

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.760
<i>High schoolers are so slender...</i>

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.540
<i>A young boy like that is 
the West representative?</i>

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.960
<i>Dr. Harada still hasn't shown up.</i>

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.650
<i>Is he using the Miyamoto Musashi strategy?</i>

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:03.330
<i>A young talent versus a seasoned veteran...</i>

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.900
<i>Who's going to win?</i>

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.750
<i>I have mixed feelings about all this,</i>

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.000
<i>so it'll be hard to back anyone 100 percent.</i>

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:20.130
<i>I guess I've grown up.</i>

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.540
<i>If I were still in grade school...</i>

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:25.640
Arata, you're amazing!

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.730
You're so close to the Master match!

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.650
You can totally do this! Keep it up!

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:32.930
<i>Will it be Arata after all?</i>

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:39.420
<i>Will he be the first to reach the stage
of the dream we talked about that day?</i>

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.980
Go get 'em, Wataya-kun!

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.950
Knock that big bear right off his feet!

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.760
It's simple, really.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.360
People only lose to him because they think 
he's an Asian black bear. It's pathetic.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.210
Think of him as a teddy bear instead!

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:59.060
Hey, Porky, why is Coach Kitano 
so hostile toward Dr. Harada?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:03.390
Not sure, but I heard something happened 
a long time ago that pissed him off.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.420
Dazaifu Karuta Society 
Certified Reader 
Makino Midori, Grade 6

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:11.410
Midori-chan! You're reading today?

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.840
Kitano-san! It's been ages!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:14.850
Doing the first match?

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.420
I'm doing the third one today.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.070
Oh, that's too bad.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.440
I sure would love to hear you read,

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.780
but I'm sure Wataya-kun will 
finish it in two matches.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.520
Really? And I came all the way from Kyushu...

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.430
But...

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.200
I do hope you're right.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.690
<i>What did Dr. Harada do?!</i>

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.520
<i>Again?</i>

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.670
<i>It's already begun.</i>

00:03:49.250 --> 00:04:01.090
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 
Sponsored by the National Karuta Association</b>

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.810
We will now begin the first match 
of the Challenger Playoffs.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.310
Thank you for the game.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.710
<i>It's so tense...</i>

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.080
You know, I never thought

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.800
the day would come when I'd 
be playing you, Glasses.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:12.170
When I was younger, I did play your grandpa,

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:15.430
Eternal Master Wataya Hajime, just once.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.590
He was good.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.730
It's a great memory.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.740
You probably can't understand yet
since you're still young,

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.250
but it brings me the greatest joy 
that I get to play you.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.620
I'll be giving these matches all I've got.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:34.370
<i>Good.</i>

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.570
<i>I'm starting to remember what wearing a 
hakama and being in a match feels like.</i>

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.340
<i>Now I just need to focus.</i>

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:47.090
<b>Good Luck, Megumu</b>

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:45.610
<i>All right.</i>

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.090
<b>Ba dump</b>

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:50.260
<b>Click Click Click Click</b>

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:50.270
<i>She usually wears it with the writing inside,
but she's showing it off today!</i>

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.390
<b>Good Luck, Megumu</b>

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:54.720
<i>Good luck, Megumu...</i>

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.870
<i>Good luck, Megumu...</i>

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:02.590
<i>No! Every time I look up at her, 
I want to say "Good luck, Megumu"!</i>

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:03.570
Time to begin.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:04.460
<i>What? Already?!</i>

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:11.950
First Match Reader 
Serizawa Taiji, Grade 6

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:06.680
Thank you for the game.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.040
Thank you for the game.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:18.970
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.960
<i>Everyone loves Serizawa-san!</i>

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.960
<i>His pitch is so precise!</i>

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:27.410
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:21.330
<i>It's starting.</i>

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.720
<i>The first match.</i>

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.340
Wait a moment, please.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.160
I think the air conditioner is still on.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.650
Could you turn it off?

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:36.770
O-Of course!

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:38.630
I'm sorry.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.610
<i>Harada!</i>

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.790
<i>Don't wait until the reading starts!</i>

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.730
<i>Are you that determined to
take control of this match?!</i>

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.740
<b>Say that sooner!</b>

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:48.860
<i>Typical Dr. Harada.</i>

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.000
<i>Typical Dr. Harada.</i>

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.330
<b>Saw that coming</b>

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.480
<i>Typical Dr. Harada.</i>

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.960
Was this a strategy, Hiroshi-san?

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.120
Yeah.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:04.370
<i>What worries me is that he might have 
done too much research on Wataya-kun.</i>

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.220
<b>Unflappable</b>

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:24.230
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 
Sponsored by the National Karuta Association</b>

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:17.800
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:25.820
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:35.200
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:43.080
<i>The hazed field of reeds conceals 
clumps of bamboo shoots,</i>

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:40.540
<i>He lunged that far on a dead card?!</i>

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:41.950
<i>S-Scary!</i>

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.710
<b>As if nothing even happened</b>

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.540
<i>May the scarlet kadsuras...</i>

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:50.840
<b>Dead card</b>

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:50.850
<i>He's lunging with his whole body! Scary!</i>

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.550
<i>Look for the sound...</i>

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.850
<b>Dead card</b>

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:52.840
<i>Scary!</i>

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:59.220
<i>The sight of the lonely 
moon in the early morning</i>

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.960
Yes! Gotcha!

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:59.240
<i>There it is! Dr. Harada's "Yes! Gotcha!"</i>

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:03.250
<i>He'd moved toward Arata-kun's 
lower right side,</i>

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.250
<i>but smoothly changed course toward the left.</i>

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.000
Arata's karuta...

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.580
is like flowing water.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.390
Like, even though he's fast, 
his movements aren't excessive.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:19.380
Flowing...

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.530
I'll just stop his flow, then.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:29.700
<i>Launch my entire upper body over to his side,</i>

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:33.130
<i>restraining my opponent...</i>

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.260
<i>and seizing aerial superiority!</i>

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:41.000
<i>He used a minimal amount of force...</i>

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.310
<i>...to take that from Arata-kun's right side!</i>

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:47.060
<i>As spirited as he is, he can 
still take cards lightly?</i>

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:51.410
<i>Dr. Harada took consecutive cards from Arata!</i>

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:55.160
<i>Wow.</i>

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.400
<i>He's so hard to play against.</i>

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.150
I'm moving my cards.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.130
<i>He moved "Since the" and 
"When I" to the left?</i>

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:13.070
<i>He's changing his layout 
this early in the game?</i>

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:16.190
<i>I thought his karuta style 
was all about balance,</i>

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:18.280
<i>but he's weighed down his left side.</i>

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:25.590
<i>When I must hide these burning feelings,</i>

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:24.310
<i>The card he moved was read immediately!</i>

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:25.590
<i>It's looking good!</i>

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:38.320
<i>...on fire with Ibuki mugwort</i>

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.320
<i>The hazed early dawn mist over the Kawagiri</i>

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.960
<b>The hazed early dawn light

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:44.950
<i>That's right! "The hazed field"
was already read!</i>

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:48.460
<i>He got a multi-syllable card 
on the second syllable...</i>

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.830
<i>With a cross?</i>

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.510
<i>At that speed?</i>

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:57.930
<i>Dr. Harada has studied Wataya-kun in depth.</i>

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.670
<i>But he only studied the old Wataya-kun.</i>

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.860
<i>How will he handle seeing a new side of him?</i>

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:13.320
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.750
<i>You probably can't understand yet
since you're still young...</i>

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:22.450
<i>Dr. Harada, you can't understand 
how I feel, either.</i>

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.910
<i>When I moved to Tokyo,</i>

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:33.130
<i>I didn't know if I'd be able to 
make friends or even play karuta.</i>

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.880
You're welcome here!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.430
I don't care what anyone else says! 
You're welcome here!

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:44.260
<i>It was like being told that
I could live life true to myself.</i>

00:09:52.230 --> 00:10:02.160
<b>You can do it!</b>

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.680
<i>He's so young,
but his movements are so efficient.</i>

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.620
<i>He arranges his cards quickly, too.</i>

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:02.150
<i>He's also been going to pick up the cards 
that Dr. Harada sends flying.</i>

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.120
<i>It's definitely clear...</i>

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:08.350
<i>...whether or not a player 
shows respect to his elders.</i>

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.040
I'm moving my cards.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.510
<i>He moved "The hazed early dawn light"
to his left, too...</i>

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:24.870
<i>Is this his response to the pressure
I've been putting on his lower right side?</i>

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:27.220
<i>He's more flexible than I realized.</i>

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:31.160
<i>Dr. Harada plays true offensive karuta.</i>

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.320
<i>He positions himself slightly left of center</i>

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:40.150
<i>so he can reach straight 
for my lower right side.</i>

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.750
<i>He intends to take every single card.</i>

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:48.480
<i>In that case, I'll split them up more.</i>

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:50.830
<i>And then...</i>

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:55.930
<i>All alone...</i>

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:57.670
<i>He...</i>

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:59.040
<i>He's fast!</i>

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.500
<i>Dr. Harada hasn't been paying 
attention to his own side...</i>

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.600
<i>There it is!</i>

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:07.030
<i>The incredible acceleration that none 
of us could reproduce in practice!</i>

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:11.770
<i>I'm happy.</i>

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.860
<i>I'm happy I get to play Dr. Harada.</i>

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:19.400
<i>I'm happy he's so strong.</i>

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:21.520
<i>But...</i>

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.850
<i>I'll be the one to win.</i>

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:37.130
<i>When the misty bridge of magpie 
feathers comes into sight,</i>

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.940
<i>Dr. Harada's upper left side...</i>

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:40.590
<i>You're playing a good, 
calm offense, Arata-kun.</i>

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:45.590
<i>Dr. Harada attacked "When winds blow," 
in Arata's upper right, on "When."</i>

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:49.940
<i>Arata stayed calm and took "When the" 
only after hearing the unique syllable.</i>

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.460
<i>He's making Dr. Harada target his right side</i>

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.850
<i>while keeping his own focus 
on the other three areas.</i>

00:11:56.470 --> 00:12:00.370
<i>And since he keeps moving his cards,
there aren't many left on his right side.</i>

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:06.320
<i>And now he sends "When winds blow," 
the one Dr. Harada was targeting!</i>

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.840
<i>He's good.</i>

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:09.820
<i>There's no doubt...</i>

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:13.680
<i>The one who has the best shot
to take down Suo Hisashi</i>

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.740
<i>is Wataya Arata.</i>

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:20.520
<i>Dr. Harada's really sweating.</i>

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:22.340
<i>It's only the middle of the match...</i>

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.960
Very good! Very good!

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:28.180
Attack him more, Wataya-kun! 
Don't let him take any!

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.890
Stop that old fool right here and now!

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:33.260
Agreed. Agreed.

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.250
I'll never forget it.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:39.160
It was at the Yoshino Tournament
 31 years ago...

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.080
<i>31 years ago?!</i>

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:48.620
<b>Me</b>

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.940
I was 26 years old.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:46.490
Wait, what? We're going 
into a flashback now?!

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:48.610
Harada and I had both won our way to the 
top with the force of a rising dragon.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.620
<b>Harada</b>

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.960
Finally, we faced each other in the finals.

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:53.990
And the original reader

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:58.640
had something else come up, so he 
was replaced at the last minute

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:04.260
I appreciate it. Thanks.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:00.230
by Kawai Midori-chan.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.190
Back then, she was my Madonna.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:04.260
<b></b>Of course

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.270
I swear I'll win!

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:08.880
I'm sorry. I yield the match.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:09.790
Huh?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:11.770
H-Hey!

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:15.330
What's your deal, Harada? Play the—

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:17.890
I don't want Kawai-san's reading 
to throw me off-kilter.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.990
Not with the Master qualifiers coming up.

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:28.750
Midori-chan later married the man 
who had comforted her that day

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:29.950
and moved to Kyushu.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.160
No!

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:35.100
And Harada, after making it as far 
as the position of challenger,

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.110
was soundly defeated in the Master match.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.420
<b><i>Serves you right!!</i></b>

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:41.500
And Midori-chan, who was such a sweet girl,

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:47.180
was driven by her bitterness toward him to
train rigorously to become a certified reader.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:52.300
An egoist who can change someone's life 
that easily ought to lose here and now!

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:55.560
Lose! Lose! Lose!

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.560
<b>Lose</b>

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.560
<b>Lose            Lose</b>

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.150
<i>It's clear from the way Arata's playing.</i>

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:11.900
<i>I'll be the one to win.</i>

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:19.930
<i>Nobody wishes to see the 
beautiful cherry blossoms</i>

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.910
<i>Good luck, Megumu! Good luck, 
Megumu! Good luck, Megumu!</i>

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.920
Click Click Click Click Click Click

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:21.740
<i>Good luck, Megumu...</i>

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:25.100
<i>No, no! I can't let her play her game!</i>

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:28.530
<i>She doesn't forget many cards.</i>

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:31.670
<i>Since she doesn't rely on game sense,
she's well-balanced.</i>

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:33.480
<i>And above all...</i>

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:38.840
<i>Serizawa-san reads with the precision of 
a metronome, and her tempo matches his.</i>

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.950
<i>It's not that Serizawa-san's reading
is difficult for me,</i>

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:44.900
<i>but it's a bit too robotic.</i>

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:49.250
<i>I thought Inokuma would have
the advantage against a high schooler,</i>

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:50.610
<i>but I guess not.</i>

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.970
<i>She lost at the Yoshino Tournament, didn't she?</i>

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:55.490
<i>And a high schooler beat her then, too.</i>

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.500
<i>A fault...</i>

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.170
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:09.850
<i>She sent me "Impassionate"? 
Is she mocking me?</i>

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:18.140
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:14.970
<i>No... She doesn't know</i>

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:17.840
<i>that my maiden name is Chihara.</i>

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:23.240
<i>Does that mean... my time has passed?</i>

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.820
<i>Go, go, Megumu! Go, go, Megumu!</i>

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:29.650
<i>Push, push, Megumu! Push, push, Megumu!</i>

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:34.770
<i>Haruka-san lost several times when
she came to practice with Fujisaki, too.</i>

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:38.260
<i>Could it be that she's gotten used to losing?</i>

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.910
<i>When she was once an invincible Queen?</i>

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:47.170
<i>Long last we meet, only for 
me to leave hurriedly,</i>

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.750
<i>He instantly took a one-syllable
on the other side!</i>

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:47.170
<i>That's to be expected.</i>

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:50.460
<i>Arata-kun's ultimate goal is Suo Hisashi.</i>

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:55.560
<i>He'll be up against a guy who claims 
he has 27 or 28 one-syllable cards.</i>

00:15:56.070 --> 00:16:00.470
<i>He's been practicing to be able to 
take all the one-syllable cards.</i>

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:05.100
<i>That speed is the result of that practice!
You've got this, Arata-kun!</i>

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:09.450
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.470
<i>My body's moving well.</i>

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:15.020
<i>I reacted perfectly.</i>

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:16.570
<i>But still...</i>

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:19.330
<i>I just barely got it.</i>

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:24.290
<i>He sent one from his right side again...</i>

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:32.860
Excuse me. I'm moving my cards.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:37.470
<i>He's moving them again because there 
aren't many left on the right?</i>

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.940
<i>He's so flexible!</i>

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:42.860
<i>If I did that, Dr. Harada 
would bite my head off.</i>

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:43.930
Chihaya-chan!

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.430
Don't change your placements!

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:49.270
If you want to move your cards, 
it has to be for a reason!

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.860
You'll be able to take more of them
if you don't move them.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.560
<i>It's the opposite for Arata.</i>

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:05.070
<i>Nothing can be worse than 
living a moment longer</i>

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:04.530
<i>That was good.</i>

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:07.690
<i>He guarded against Wataya while going 
for the "None are" on Wataya's side,</i>

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:09.080
<i>but went back to "Nothing."</i>

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:15.460
<i>While the autumn leaves of Mount Ogura 
would never understand human emotion,</i>

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:16.600
<i>His upper body reacted to "While it brings"
on Wataya's lower right,</i>

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.810
<i>but his hand smoothly reached 
for "While the" on his own side!</i>

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:25.240
<i>The fall wind parts...</i>

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:26.240
<i>Dr. Harada's defense on his 
own side is incredible, too!</i>

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:30.550
<i>There's no doubt he's attacking 
his opponent's lower right side.</i>

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.440
<i>But he's only leaning
toward that right side,</i>

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:38.060
<i>which makes it possible 
for him to change course.</i>

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:42.200
<i>If his arm was also reaching for that side,
he couldn't move that way.</i>

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:43.910
<i>He's...</i>

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:48.780
<i>moving his arm as little as possible 
to avoid building up inertia!</i>

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:50.870
<i>So on the unique syllable...</i>

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:54.440
<i>he can move freely!</i>

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:56.540
Hup...

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:02.510
<i>It's a type of karuta that youngsters
with active bodies can't play.</i>

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:09.320
<i>Wataya-kun may have the momentum, 
but he can't pull far ahead.</i>

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:18.350
<i>When winds blow oak leaves in the twilight,</i>

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:17.690
<i>He nailed "When winds blow," 
the card he sent me.</i>

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:19.190
<i>He really is fast.</i>

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.710
<i>But even Glasses...</i>

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:27.800
<i>can't take every single card at that speed.</i>

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.110
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:35.450
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:37.220
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:39.020
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:45.000
<i>I've been a mentor for a long time.</i>

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:49.760
You'll be able to take more of them
if you don't move them.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:53.740
<i>I have a duty to prove that to you!</i>

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:55.240
All right! I got in!

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.450
Thank you very much.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.960
Thank you very much.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.590
The first match goes to Dr. Harada!

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:20.340
<i>Good luck, Megumu! Good luck, Megumu!</i>

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.790
<i>Good luck, Megumu! Good luck, Megumu!</i>

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:23.550
<i>Good luck...</i>

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.020
<i>Good luck, me!</i>

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:31.190
<i>Inokuma-san just barely won by two cards!</i>

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.890
<i>The veterans took both games!</i>

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:33.690
<i>Amazing!</i>

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:38.960
<i>Karuta is not about youth or momentum.</i>

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:50.710
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 
Sponsored by the National Karuta Association</b>

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:46.880
The second match will begin at 12:30,
after the lunch break.

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:50.710
Participants, please be in 
your seats by that time.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.010
I knew Dr. Harada could do it.

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:56.090
It feels good to see a veteran 
showing his strength.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.220
<i>I don't want to admit it,</i>

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:03.990
<i>but there's no one else past age fifty
with the will and stamina</i>

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:05.760
<i>to go for the Master title.</i>

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:09.540
<i>Not that I'm ever going to cheer for him.</i>

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.350
Oh, excuse me.

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:13.580
I'd like to withdraw from the second match.

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.360
What?!

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.470
I'll be back for the third match.

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:19.610
Pardon me.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:35.830
You're reading for the third match,
right, Makino-san?

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.410
Right now, rather than Igarashi-san, 
who's doing the second match...

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:44.880
I much prefer your reading.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:55.650
<i>I swear I will never cheer you on!
Drop dead, Harada!</i>

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.560
Withdrawing?

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:00.850
Does that mean he gets a win 
without even doing anything?

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:08.900
<i>He's toying with you, Arata-kun!</i>

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:09.910
Arata.
